{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/466683-w-tf-2e-bristol-s-gull-clan","id":466683,"title":"[W:tF 2e] Bristol's Gull Clan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-02T17:13:51-07:00","id":466683,"title":"[W:tF 2e] Bristol's Gull Clan","content":"So as anyone who has read the Hunting Grounds chapter of Werewolf 2e knows there is a great oddity in the Bristol, England setting.<br /> <br /> A so-called clan of vampire known as the Gull. They are modern day slavers who potentially have a literal ghost ship at their disposal, and who essentially control the suburb of Avonmouth as far as supernatural activity goes.<br /> <br /> Has anyone done any development or had any thoughts on this particular oddity introduced in another gameline entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T18:46:23-07:00","id":466799,"title":"","content":"I hadn't thought of them as their own clan, I thought it was referring to clan as in the more local family sense. One vampire and their 'descendants.'<br /> <br /> But I suppose that makes sense. They may be something the idigam Afzu\u2019Umm\u2019Ia created or something already created that it took advantage of. It would certainly be cool to see a clan write-up for them like the Jiang-shi. I don't think they'd be considered a true clan, but they'd have some weird disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:05:35-07:00","id":466846,"title":"","content":"It could be either the 'local family' sense or the 'actual clan' sense. Either way it would be nice to see some thought put into it. Like if they are 'just' a local dynasty, what Clan are they? Do Covenants enter into the picture for them? Are they a Bloodline in their own right?<br /> <br /> If they're an actual clan, what kind of Disciplines and Banes would they have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:21:54-07:00","id":466873,"title":"","content":"I imagine it's probably a lineage being colorfully described as a clan. Either way, that adds some character to the area! Did it say how long they've been there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:25:23-07:00","id":466875,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Idigam in the area has Twist Blood as a Dread Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:29:16-07:00","id":466878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/466683-w-tf-2e-bristol-s-gull-clan?p=466873#post466873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine it's probably a lineage being colorfully described as a clan. Either way, that adds some character to the area! Did it say how long they've been there?</div> </div> </div> </div>At minimum before 1709 C.E. Possibly older; the clan originated with Bristol's slave trade, and the first of them may have rose from the crew of some slave ships. Nobody's sure why they just kinda rose from deaths by violence or disease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:35:56-07:00","id":466890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/466683-w-tf-2e-bristol-s-gull-clan?p=466873#post466873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did it say how long they've been there?</div> </div> </div> </div>'As far as the Uratha can tell, the first of these vampires rose amongst the crew of slave-ships, though what caused sailors killed by violence or disease to rise again is a mystery.' A quick and possibly inaccurate google search tells me that <a href=\"http://discoveringbristol.org.uk/slavery/routes/bristol-to-africa/shipping/bristols-slave-ships/\" target=\"_blank\">this period ranges from 1698 to 1807</a>.<br /> <br /> The thing that gets me is this line, 'Whispered rumors have it that when the sea is cloaked in fog, the captain sails once more in the creaking, rotting hulk of his ship, attended by a court of weeping ghosts chained to his will.' This makes me think whatever it is, it's not solely a vampire. Because this is something an idigam can do, chain ghosts to their will. It's possible the idigam has used Forge Herald on it, which could give it the Soul Slave Dread Power, which would account for a court of weeping 'ghosts.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-02-2015, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T19:44:47-07:00","id":466896,"title":"","content":"Oh. Well then.<br /> <br /> We're screwed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T00:47:32-07:00","id":468182,"title":"","content":"Probably not.<br /> <br /> First of all, forge herald only works on werewolves and humans, vampires aren't either. Of course, nothing stopping an idigam to make a new version for vampires.<br /> <br /> Even if they did so though, by captured ghosts, do you mean soul slave? Soul slaves require captured souls, so how is this vampire capturing souls to enslave? Forge herald only grants one dread power, and the idea that the idigam collects souls so that the vampire herald can enslave them seems a little weird, don't you think? <br /> <br /> So occam's razor, the gull clan are probably either a necromantic bloodline, or members of a blood cult that grants necromantic powers. <br /> <br /> I'm all for the idigam playing with vampires, but this case seems a little far fetched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T01:16:38-07:00","id":468206,"title":"","content":"Forge Herald doesn't say it's only limited to werewolves and humans. And the soul slave Dread Power seems to allow capture of the souls itself. Occam's Razor would suggest since there's a unique vampire clan in the same ocean as an idigam that can create unique things that it is not a previously unheard vampire clan with previously unknown abilities or a cult of which there's no mention whatsoever.<br /> <br /> You're free to do whatever you want with it but it certainly isn't far fetched to have the idigam that lives in the same waters involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-04-2015, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T08:16:58-07:00","id":470159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/466683-w-tf-2e-bristol-s-gull-clan?p=466890#post466890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'As far as the Uratha can tell, the first of these vampires rose amongst the crew of slave-ships, though what caused sailors killed by violence or disease to rise again is a mystery.' A quick and possibly inaccurate google search tells me that <a href=\"http://discoveringbristol.org.uk/slavery/routes/bristol-to-africa/shipping/bristols-slave-ships/\" target=\"_blank\">this period ranges from 1698 to 1807</a>.<br /> <br /> The thing that gets me is this line, 'Whispered rumors have it that when the sea is cloaked in fog, the captain sails once more in the creaking, rotting hulk of his ship, attended by a court of weeping ghosts chained to his will.' This makes me think whatever it is, it's not solely a vampire. Because this is something an idigam can do, chain ghosts to their will. It's possible the idigam has used Forge Herald on it, which could give it the Soul Slave Dread Power, which would account for a court of weeping 'ghosts.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I fancy making them older. The Anglo-Saxons of Bristol sold British slaves to the Vikings and it didn't stop altogether when it was banned. And if they were Weihan Cynn, maybe they had a few necromancer friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T07:53:56-07:00","id":476946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/466683-w-tf-2e-bristol-s-gull-clan?p=468206#post468206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forge Herald doesn't say it's only limited to werewolves and humans. And the soul slave Dread Power seems to allow capture of the souls itself. Occam's Razor would suggest since there's a unique vampire clan in the same ocean as an idigam that can create unique things that it is not a previously unheard vampire clan with previously unknown abilities or a cult of which there's no mention whatsoever.<br /> <br /> You're free to do whatever you want with it but it certainly isn't far fetched to have the idigam that lives in the same waters involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>What of &quot;By targeting humans or uratha&quot; is supposed to be open to interpretation here?<br /> <br /> Or &quot;A herald follows the usual rules for a human or werewolf...?&quot;<br /> <br /> And no soul slave doesn't allow capturing souls, it allows one to do something with a captured soul.<br /> <br /> &quot;Some forge servant powers remove the target's soul...may store it. An idigam may retain up to twice its rank in stored souis.&quot;<br /> <br /> So again, even if forge herald worked on vampires, which it doesn't, the vampire herald would have no powers to collect souls because soul slave doesn't give one the power to capture souls, which makes it a weird choice to give said herald, since the idigam would have to collect the souls for the servant, making it an odd choice.<br /> <br /> Well except for diablorie, I suppose the gulls could diablorize vampires to gain new ghost servants, but considering the downsides of diablorie that doesn't seem like an ability one would use a whole lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 04-11-2015, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T12:44:33-07:00","id":477181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/466683-w-tf-2e-bristol-s-gull-clan?p=476946#post476946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What of &quot;By targeting humans or uratha&quot; is supposed to be open to interpretation here?<br /> Or &quot;A herald follows the usual rules for a human or werewolf...?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically whether or not vampires are human. Uratha are another race entirely. Vampires are undead humans. It doesn't say mortals or living.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well except for diablorie, I suppose the gulls could diablorize vampires to gain new ghost servants, but considering the downsides of diablorie that doesn't seem like an ability one would use a whole lot. </div> </div> </div>There's a discipline that allows for the removal of souls, too. And a variety of ways to avoid the humanity loss from diablerie. But it's also possible the herald isn't sitting there alone on a ghost ship doing nothing, and their idigam is with them, with the souls belonging to it. Or the soul slaves may be the idigams, and ordered to watch and keep guard over the vampire, perhaps it has a merit that allows it to drink Vitae from them so it doesn't have to leave the ocean. It could be any number of things supported by the rules and the fluff of the game, or even beyond them.<br /> <br /> 'The idigam are diverse beings once Coalesced, capable of all manner of bizarre and unnatural accomplishments. Storytellers are encouraged to create new Essence Shaping powers that match the themes and role of an idigam in their chronicle.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-11-2015, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T18:25:45-07:00","id":477422,"title":"","content":"Aye, I would say that the sheer awesome creepy factor of an Idigam controlling a small bloodline of Vampires with the ability to enslave ghosts is awesome enough that it has to be a thing. Maybe only the elder of the line knows the Idigam is pulling the strings, the younger vampires don't know the truth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}